sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch01-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch01-10--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch01-10--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch01-10: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.82" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.825"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.83"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The named ancestor and the alternative of several wild stocks are both directly readable from public pigeon and Columba sequences. Major breed groups and the rock-pigeon have already been deposited, so a reanalysis is weeks of standard phylogenomics rather than a new collecting program. Incomplete sampling of obscure breeds and wild subspecies limits certainty at the margin and does not block a confirm-or-refute test of the stated origin." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Place domestic pigeon breeds and wild Columba species, including geographical forms of Columba livia, on a multilocus tree and an admixture graph. Nesting of all breed groups inside C. livia would support single origin from the rock-pigeon; breed groups scattered among other wild Columba species would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Not every fancy breed and not every geographical subspecies of C. livia is sequenced.", "Feral pigeons and later hybridization can obscure an originally mixed origin.", "A few breeds differ by large-effect mutations, which does not by itself imply a different wild species." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch01-10--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch01-10--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch01-10--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch01-10--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch01-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.93" ;
